      "characterId": "fern-longnose",
      "identityNameBase": "Fern Longnose",
      "subject": "white-nosed coati",
      "scientificName": "Nasua narica",
      "title": "Two occupied paws",
      "theme": "feeding",
      "photoId": 121137270,
      "body": "Pulled the sweet thing closer. It tipped, and a drop ran down my wrist.\n\nLicked my wrist. Lost the rim.\n\nCaught it again. Now both paws are wet and I have to choose between holding breakfast and licking it off myself.",
      "fictionBoundary": "Feeder, liquid reservoir, tipped red rim, coati mouth and both gripping forepaws are visible. Sweetness, spilling onto the wrist, licking, loss and recovery of grip are fiction. No photographed sequence or chemical analysis is claimed. No free-hanging body: hind feet remain supported by the stump. No claim that this feeder is in wild forest or that a human appears offering food.",
      "canon": "Existing adult female Fern; source sex unspecified. Keep Corcovado lowland forest home8.54,-83.57 and current avatar. Source Arizona is provenance. Append as independent adult incident after the admitted unfinished-foot scene; no new offspring, group abandonment or late-arrival joke.",
      "payoff": "The same paws that secure access become the competing place where she wants to eat. This is a grip/licking conflict, not finding food or arguing about its quality.",
      "platform": "instagram",
      "contentType": "story",
      "mediaSha1": "62328b2755b147737effe8278a9e7b6d6fc69b0f",
