    },
    {
      "characterId": "aster-reed",
      "identityNameBase": "Aster Reed",
      "subject": "common darter dragonfly",
      "scientificName": "Sympetrum striolatum",
      "title": "Resting place",
      "theme": "movement",
      "photoId": 51622892,
      "body": "The reed is gone. Stopped above the place anyway.\n\nHeld there. Slipped sideways. Came back.\n\nI used to rest here. Today I'm using all four wings to do it.",
      "fictionBoundary": "Red darter and all four wings in active flight are visible. Hovering at a remembered perch location, loss of a reed and the small correction sequence are fiction. No broken reed is claimed visible. The image carries the active flight replacing supported rest; species identification comes from research-grade primary record and API taxon55625, not from wing blur alone.",
      "canon": "Existing male adult common darter, red adult compatible with BDS male comparison. Keep New Forest pond margin50.855,-1.624 and current avatar. Source Berlin remains provenance. This recovers the still-held loss-of-perch premise as a separate proposed replacement, not an additional duplicate. Place after any earlier reed-claim episodes if those are admitted later. Do not silently reinstate the old literal draft.",
      "payoff": "He insists on occupying the exact place of rest and spends sustained effort doing so. Body ends on the four wings at work, not an abstract attachment lesson.",
      "imageFlag": "Motion gives the scene its point, but body/eye detail is softer than the static macro. Root should independently judge this exact delivery rather than infer quality from other photos.",
      "platform": "instagram",
