      "localPath": "/tmp/freed-land100/51622892.jpg"
    },
    {
      "characterId": "sable-crest",
      "identityNameBase": "Sable Crest",
      "subject": "secretary bird",
      "scientificName": "Sagittarius serpentarius",
      "title": "A movement beside me",
      "theme": "danger",
      "photoId": 512826107,
      "body": "Something moved beside my face. Stepped back. It came with me.\n\nTook another step before I remembered the bit of lunch still hanging from my bill.\n\nFinished swallowing. Looked at the bush again. I had moved quite a long way for something I was already eating.",
      "fictionBoundary": "Secretary bird holds a long narrow prey animal curving near its bill, beside thorny vegetation. Source identifies the bird as eater. No prey species, venom or distress state assigned. Motion, startle, backward steps, recognition and swallowing sequence are fictional. Companion frames show long prey then near-closed bill, but are not claimed to prove the imagined reaction. The shrub is a visible reference point, not a claimed snag.",
      "canon": "Existing adult female Sable, photographed sex unrecorded. Keep Serengeti grasslands,-2.543,34.822 and current avatar. Source Tanzania compatible but not proof of this exact home. Append after Measured force as a distinct adult incident: an automatic retreat while she retains lunch, not another missed kick. Preserve all held literal snake/crest episodes.",
      "payoff": "The movement she retreats from is travelling with her because she is already eating it. No triumphant joke about prey suffering, injury or named antagonist.",
